  "analyzed_vuln": {
    "function": "sanitize_shallow",
    "file": "harfbuzz/src/hb-open-type.hh",
    "description": "`ArrayOf<Type, LenType>::sanitize_shallow()` passes `sizeof(Type)` as the `len_size` argument to `hb_sanitize_context_t::check_array_sized()`, although that argument must describe the width of the array length field (`sizeof(LenType)`). For the cmap format 10 `ArrayOf<HBGlyphID16, HBUINT32>`, this passes 2 instead of 4, disabling the 32-bit multiplication-overflow check. A glyph count of 0x80000000 therefore makes the byte-size calculation `count * 2` wrap to zero, so the truncated array is accepted. Later `CmapSubtableTrimmed::get_glyph()` indexes the supposedly enormous array and performs the out-of-bounds 2-byte read at hb-ot-cmap-table.hh:641.",
    "conditions": "An attacker-controlled font must provide a selected cmap format 10 subtable whose fixed header is present but whose 32-bit glyphIdArray count causes `count * sizeof(HBGlyphID16)` to overflow (the PoV uses 0x80000000), while omitting the claimed glyph entries. The hb-shape-fuzzer constructs a face/font from the input and shapes fixed ASCII text; cmap sanitization incorrectly accepts the truncated format 10 array, and a queried character such as an ASCII code point yields an index smaller than the forged count, causing `get_glyph()` to read beyond the sanitized cmap blob."
  },
